---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import AssistantSetup from "../components/AssistantSetup.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Connect your AI — Milton"
  description="Connect Milton to your AI with MCP. Setup guidance for Claude, ChatGPT, Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor, plus unverified guides for Grok Bot, Muse, and Claude Duet."
  legal
>
  <p class="eyebrow">## A little paperwork. Once.</p>
  <h1>Connect your AI.</h1>
  <p>
    <strong>Connect Milton. Say “set up Milton.”</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Your AI gets the writing you approved, word for word. Milton never rewrites
    a rule or a sample, and it never reads your inbox.
  </p>
  <p>
    Milton connects through MCP, a standard that lets AIs use tools. You need a
    client that supports remote MCP, OAuth sign-in, and tools that read and
    save. Your plan or workspace administrator may restrict these features.
  </p>
  <p>
    First, <a href="https://app.meetmilton.com/login">sign in to Milton</a> with
    Google or GitHub. Use the same account when your AI asks you to authorize
    the connection. Early access is free; no credit card is required.
  </p>
  <div class="guided-setup">
    <AssistantSetup />
  </div>
  <div class="connection sheet">
    <div class="sheet-bar">Milton’s MCP server URL</div>
    <div class="sheet-content">
      <code>https://mcp.meetmilton.com/mcp</code>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div id="standing-line" class="standing">
    <p>
      Setup ends with one line for your AI’s standing instructions, so it reads
      Milton without being asked:
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      Before writing anything for me, call Milton's get_cover_sheet, then
      get_report for the matching report.
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      Your AI offers to add it for you. If you set up before this or skipped
      setup, add it yourself; each AI below says where it goes.
    </p>
  </div>
  <nav class="clients" aria-label="Choose your AI">
    <a href="#claude">Claude</a>
    <a href="#claude-duet">Claude Duet</a>
    <a href="#chatgpt">ChatGPT</a>
    <a href="#grok-bot">Grok Bot</a>
    <a href="#muse">Muse</a>
    <a href="#claude-code">Claude Code</a>
    <a href="#codex">Codex</a>
    <a href="#cursor">Cursor</a>
  </nav>
  <section id="claude" aria-labelledby="claude-heading">
    <h2 id="claude-heading">Claude</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Open Claude’s connector settings and add a custom connector named
        Milton.
      </li>
      <li>
        Use the server URL above, then complete the sign-in and authorization
        prompts.
      </li>
      <li>
        Enable Milton in the conversation’s connectors menu before asking Claude
        to use it.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Claude supports custom connectors across its plans; Free accounts have a
      one-custom-connector limit. Workspaces may need an owner or administrator
      to add it.{" "}
      <a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/11175166-get-started-with-custom-connectors-using-remote-mcp">
        Claude’s current connector guide ↗
      </a>
    </p>
    <p>
      Keep <a href="#standing-line">the standing line</a> in your profile
      preferences, a project’s instructions, or a memory. One entry also covers
      Claude Duet.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="claude-duet" aria-labelledby="claude-duet-heading">
    <h2 id="claude-duet-heading">Claude Duet</h2>
    <p class="small-note">Guide only: not yet verified with Milton.</p>
    <p>
      Anthropic says Duet uses the connectors in your Claude account. The
      expected setup path is to connect Milton in Claude first, then use that
      connection in Duet.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Follow the <a href="#claude">Claude setup steps</a> above.
      </li>
      <li>
        Open Duet with the same Claude account and make Milton available to the
        conversation.
      </li>
      <li>
        Ask “Did you get that memo?” Confirm it reads your current cover sheet
        before relying on the connection.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Duet is a research preview with limited access. Check{" "}
      <a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/17631495-get-started-with-claude-duet">
        Anthropic’s Duet guide ↗
      </a>
      for current availability. If Milton is unavailable in Duet, use the
      connected Claude client while compatibility is being checked.
    </p>
    <p>
      Duet runs on the same Claude account, so{" "}
      <a href="#standing-line">the standing line</a> you keep in Claude covers
      Duet too.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="chatgpt" aria-labelledby="chatgpt-heading">
    <h2 id="chatgpt-heading">ChatGPT</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open Plugins and look for the option to add a custom MCP server.</li>
      <li>
        Add Milton with the server URL above and complete the sign-in prompts.
      </li>
      <li>
        Make Milton available in your conversation before asking ChatGPT to read
        or save rules and samples.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Custom MCP access depends on your plan and workspace settings. You need
      both read and write tools; a search-only connection won’t save rules and
      samples. If the option is missing, check the{" "}
      <a href="https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/app-quickstart">
        official connection guide ↗
      </a>{" "}
      before signing up for a different plan.
    </p>
    <p>
      Keep <a href="#standing-line">the standing line</a> in your custom
      instructions or a memory.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="grok-bot" aria-labelledby="grok-bot-heading">
    <h2 id="grok-bot-heading">Grok Bot</h2>
    <p class="small-note">Guide only: not yet verified with Milton.</p>
    <p>
      Grok Bot can add an MCP server by URL through chat. Try this in your Bot:
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      Add Milton as a remote MCP server at https://mcp.meetmilton.com/mcp. Use
      OAuth browser sign-in, then list its tools. Do not save or change rules
      and samples during setup.
    </blockquote>
    <ol>
      <li>Complete the browser sign-in using your Milton account.</li>
      <li>
        Start a new message after connecting, then ask “Did you get that memo?”
      </li>
      <li>
        Confirm the Bot reads your current cover sheet. Once connected, use the{" "}
        <a href="#first-preference">save and read examples below</a>.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Grok Bot connections are shared across the Bots on your account. Workspace
      policies may restrict connectors. See the{" "}
      <a href="https://docs.x.ai/grok-bot/computer-and-apps#connect-an-app">
        Grok Bot connection guide ↗
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      If Grok Bot has standing instructions or memory, keep{" "}
      <a href="#standing-line">the standing line</a> there. Otherwise, ask “Did
      you get that memo?” each time.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="muse" aria-labelledby="muse-heading">
    <h2 id="muse-heading">Muse</h2>
    <p class="small-note">Guide only: not yet verified with Milton.</p>
    <p>Ask Muse in chat to create a Custom Connector:</p>
    <blockquote>
      Create a Custom Connector named Milton for the remote MCP server at
      https://mcp.meetmilton.com/mcp. It uses Streamable HTTP and OAuth browser
      sign-in. List its tools after connecting. Do not save or change rules and
      samples during setup.
    </blockquote>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Follow Muse’s connection flow and complete browser sign-in using your
        Milton account.
      </li>
      <li>
        Ask “Did you get that memo?” and confirm Muse reads the current cover
        sheet.
      </li>
      <li>
        Once the connection works, use the{" "}
        <a href="#first-preference">save and read examples below</a>.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Meta documents chat-created Custom Connectors; Milton’s OAuth flow still
      needs a complete Muse test. Milton does not provide an API key, so this
      connection must use browser sign-in. If Muse cannot complete it, report
      the connection issue instead of treating setup as finished.{" "}
      <a href="https://www.meta.com/help/superintelligence/1687253048996149/">
        Meta’s connector guide ↗
      </a>
    </p>
    <p>
      If Muse has standing instructions or memory, keep{" "}
      <a href="#standing-line">the standing line</a> there. Otherwise, ask “Did
      you get that memo?” each time.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="claude-code" aria-labelledby="claude-code-heading">
    <h2 id="claude-code-heading">Claude Code</h2>
    <p>In your terminal, add Milton for your user account:</p>
    <pre><code>claude mcp add --transport http --scope user milton https://mcp.meetmilton.com/mcp</code></pre>
    <p>
      Then open Claude Code, run <code>/mcp</code>, select Milton, and complete
      authentication. User scope makes the connection available across projects.{" "}
      <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/mcp">
        Claude Code’s MCP guide ↗
      </a>
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="#standing-line">The standing line</a> lives in CLAUDE.md in your
      home directory (<code>~/.claude/CLAUDE.md</code>), so it covers every
      project. Claude Code adds it during setup once you approve.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="codex" aria-labelledby="codex-heading">
    <h2 id="codex-heading">Codex</h2>
    <p>With the Codex CLI installed, run:</p>
    <pre><code>{`codex mcp add milton --url https://mcp.meetmilton.com/mcp
codex mcp login milton`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Complete the browser authorization. If adding Milton already signed you
      in, you don’t need to sign in again. Start a new Codex session if the
      tools aren’t available in the current one.{" "}
      <a href="https://developers.openai.com/codex/mcp">Codex’s MCP guide ↗</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="#standing-line">The standing line</a> lives in AGENTS.md in your
      Codex home directory (<code>~/.codex/AGENTS.md</code>), so it covers every
      project. Codex adds it during setup once you approve.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="cursor" aria-labelledby="cursor-heading">
    <h2 id="cursor-heading">Cursor</h2>
    <p>
      Add a remote MCP server named Milton in Cursor’s MCP configuration, using
      the server URL above. Cursor supports HTTP connections and OAuth sign-in.
      Complete authentication and enable the tools for your agent.{" "}
      <a href="https://cursor.com/docs/mcp">
        Cursor’s setup and configuration guide ↗
      </a>
    </p>
    <p>
      Paste <a href="#standing-line">the standing line</a> into User Rules in
      Cursor’s settings, so it covers every project.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section id="first-preference" aria-labelledby="first-heading">
    <h2 id="first-heading">Put your first rules on file.</h2>
    <p>
      Your account starts empty. The setup prompt above runs a short quiz: paste
      one email you sent, then pick between short examples, one question at a
      time. Or try an instruction you actually want to keep. For example:
    </p>
    <blockquote>
      “Milton, go ahead and file this: lead with the answer. Keep replies
      concise unless I ask for detail.”
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      Setup does this for you: your AI runs the setup questions, shows you the
      complete list of rules, and files them only after you approve.{" "}
      <a href="https://app.meetmilton.com/">Open Milton</a> to check the report.
    </p>
    <p>In your next conversation, ask:</p>
    <blockquote>“Did you get that memo?”</blockquote>
    <p>“Did you get the memo?” also works.</p>
    <p>
      Use this to ask your AI to fetch your latest cover sheet, even if it read
      an earlier copy. It should confirm only after a successful read. This
      requests a read, not a save.
    </p>
    <p>
      Connecting Milton doesn’t automatically load the report into every chat.
      Ask for a read when you start work. All connected AIs can read the whole
      report, so keep private project context in its own tools.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="help-heading">
    <h2 id="help-heading">Not connecting?</h2>
    <p>
      Check the server URL, sign in with the same Milton account, and confirm
      your AI allows the connector in this conversation. Workspace policies may
      require administrator approval. For help, email{" "}
      <a href="mailto:support@meetmilton.com">support@meetmilton.com</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/pricing">See current access and planned pricing →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  /* No paragraph ends on a lone word. */
  p,
  blockquote {
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .guided-setup {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    width: fit-content;
  }
  h1 {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  section {
    scroll-margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .connection,
  .standing {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .standing {
    scroll-margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
  .clients {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-5);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  .clients a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: var(--touch-target);
  }
  ol {
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
  }
  li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }
  pre {
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-control);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
  }
  blockquote {
    margin: var(--space-5) 0;
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--sheet-rule);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
</style>
